# Base URL of the FastAPI backend. Must start with EXPO_PUBLIC_ so Expo inlines it
# into the app bundle (see https://docs.expo.dev/guides/environment-variables/).
#
# - Web build / iOS simulator on the SAME machine as the backend: 127.0.0.1 works.
# - Physical phone (Expo Go or a dev build): 127.0.0.1 does NOT work — it resolves
#   to the phone itself. Use your computer's LAN IP instead, e.g.:
#     EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.13:8000
#   (find yours with `ipconfig` on Windows / `ifconfig`|`ip addr` on macOS/Linux;
#   phone and computer must be on the same network, and the backend must be started
#   with a host that isn't just 127.0.0.1, e.g. `uvicorn app.main:app --host 0.0.0.0`)
# - Android emulator: the emulator's own loopback alias for the host machine is
#   typically 10.0.2.2 (AVD/Android Studio emulator) — this depends on which
#   emulator you're using; check its docs if 10.0.2.2 doesn't work.
#
# Copy this file to .env and edit the value — .env is gitignored, no secrets live
# in this app either way.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
